WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.493
Sara was fond of the Large family because they looked happy.

2
00:00:16.494 --> 00:00:21.321
But she liked the gentleman next door because he looked unhappy.

3
00:00:21.322 --> 00:00:25.233
The school's servants were always talking about him.

4
00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:30.640
Sara learned that the English gentleman had become ill after losing his fortune.

5
00:00:30.641 --> 00:00:34.818
He'd gotten his fortune back, but he was still sick.

6
00:00:34.819 --> 00:00:39.701
"His problems were connected with diamond mines," said the cook.

7
00:00:39.702 --> 00:00:45.959
She glanced at Sara. "We all know they're trouble."

8
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.596
"That man was just like Papa," Sara said to herself.

9
00:00:50.597 --> 00:00:55.729
"He felt just what my Papa felt, only he did not die."

10
00:00:55.730 --> 00:01:01.678
So Sara grew even fonder of the sick gentleman next door.

11
00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:06.067
Whenever she was sent out at night, she stopped outside his house.

12
00:01:06.068 --> 00:01:12.665
She liked to peek into the house and see him sitting in his armchair, his forehead resting in his hand.

13
00:01:12.666 --> 00:01:15.534
She often wished him good night.

14
00:01:15.535 --> 00:01:21.519
"Perhaps you can feel my good wishes even if you can't hear them," she said.

15
00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:28.320
"I hope you'll get well and be happy again. I'm so sorry for you."

16
00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:33.412
She went on her way, feeling comforted and a bit warmer herself.

17
00:01:33.413 --> 00:01:36.533
But she kept worrying about the man.

18
00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:41.659
He looked to Sara like someone who had a lot of trouble on his mind.

19
00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:47.906
Meanwhile Mr. Large and his daughters Janet and Nora often visited the gentleman.

20
00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:54.735
The sick man's name was Mr. Carrisford. Mr. Large's real name was Mr. Carmichael.

21
00:01:54.736 --> 00:01:57.671
He was Mr. Carrisford's lawyer.

22
00:01:57.672 --> 00:02:03.966
One evening Janet told Mr. Carrisford about the Little Girl Who Is Not a Beggar.

23
00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:07.325
He was very interested.

24
00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:11.501
Then Ram Dass told him the story of the monkey's escape.

25
00:02:11.502 --> 00:02:18.010
Ram Dass described the servant girl's cold attic room and her hard, narrow bed.

26
00:02:18.011 --> 00:02:21.310
The story upset Mr. Carrisford.

27
00:02:21.311 --> 00:02:26.867
He was wealthy and comfortable while children were cold and hungry.

28
00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:33.233
"I wonder how many of the attics in London are like that one," he said to Mr. Carmichael.

29
00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:39.596
"How many young servant girls sleep on hard beds while I sleep on soft pillows?"

30
00:02:39.597 --> 00:02:44.485
"My dear fellow," Mr. Carmichael answered in a cheery voice.

31
00:02:44.486 --> 00:02:47.335
"You must stop thinking thoughts like this.

32
00:02:47.336 --> 00:02:52.310
Even if you had all the wealth in the world, you could not improve all the attics in London.

33
00:02:52.311 --> 00:02:56.076
You must focus your thoughts on becoming well."

34
00:02:56.077 --> 00:03:01.402
Mr. Carrisford sat and bit his nails as he stared into the fire.

35
00:03:01.403 --> 00:03:07.372
"Do you think the girl I'm looking for is living in such a horrid place?" he asked suddenly.

36
00:03:07.373 --> 00:03:10.660
Mr. Carmichael looked at him uneasily.

37
00:03:10.661 --> 00:03:16.064
He knew that this kind of thinking was very dangerous to the frail gentleman's health.

38
00:03:16.065 --> 00:03:20.474
"I don't think so," he said finally in a soothing tone.

39
00:03:20.475 --> 00:03:24.455
"That girl was adopted by a wealthy Russian couple."

40
00:03:24.456 --> 00:03:28.509
"I must find her!" Mr. Carrisford went on.

41
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.318
"If she is friendless and penniless, it is my fault!

42
00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:36.559
She is the daughter of my dear friend, Captain Crewe."

43
00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:42.206
"Are you sure his daughter was sent to boarding school in France?" Mr. Carmichael asked.

44
00:03:42.207 --> 00:03:45.574
"Perhaps we're searching for the wrong girl."

45
00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:50.736
"I'm not sure of anything." Mr. Carrisford bit his nails again.

46
00:03:50.737 --> 00:03:53.638
"Crewe and I talked mainly about the mines.

47
00:03:53.639 --> 00:03:58.514
Her mother was French, so I assumed she went to a French school."

48
00:03:58.515 --> 00:04:06.056
"The French headmistress pronounced the student's name Carew instead of Crewe," Mr. Carmichael reminded him.

49
00:04:06.057 --> 00:04:10.081
"So it's possible that we are on the trail of the wrong girl."

50
00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:12.571
"We must find Crewe's daughter!"

51
00:04:12.572 --> 00:04:18.408
Mr. Carrisford clutched Mr. Carmichael's arm. "Help me find her!"

52
00:04:18.409 --> 00:04:21.695
"Don't worry," said Mr. Carmichael.

53
00:04:21.696 --> 00:04:24.073
"I'll go to Moscow to look for the girl.

54
00:04:24.074 --> 00:04:28.068
If she's not the right girl, we will keep searching."

55
00:04:28.069 --> 00:04:32.805
"If I were able to travel, I would go with you," said Mr. Carrisford.

56
00:04:32.806 --> 00:04:39.850
"But I am too ill. I can only sit here wrapped in fur and staring at the fire.

57
00:04:39.851 --> 00:04:43.817
And when I look into it, I see Crewe's face gazing back at me.

58
00:04:43.818 --> 00:04:49.284
And he's asking me a question: 'Tom, where is my little girl?'"

59
00:04:49.285 --> 00:04:53.684
Mr. Carrisford grabbed Mr. Carmichael's hand desperately.

60
00:04:53.685 --> 00:04:58.065
"I must be able to answer him!"

61
00:04:58.066 --> 00:05:04.061
On the other side of the wall, Sara was sitting in her room, talking to Mel the rat.

62
00:05:04.062 --> 00:05:09.394
"It was very hard to be a princess today, Mel," she said.

63
00:05:09.395 --> 00:05:14.263
"It gets harder as the weather gets colder and the streets get wetter."

64
00:05:14.264 --> 00:05:19.662
Lavinia had laughed at Sara's skirt, spattered with mud from the street.

65
00:05:19.663 --> 00:05:23.854
But Sara had not responded.

66
00:05:23.855 --> 00:05:30.578
"You can't snap at people if you're a princess," she explained to the rat.

67
00:05:30.579 --> 00:05:36.466
"But it was such a cold afternoon. And it's so cold tonight."

68
00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:41.969
Sara put her head in her lap. "Oh, Papa," she whispered.

69
00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:51.642
"It seems like such a long time since I was your little girl!"
